  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK domestic poverty</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will support influencing, programmatic, and partnership work initiatives to challenge the inequalities that fuel poverty in the UK, in support of Oxfam&apos;s strategic priorities and ensuring alignment with (1) work in Wales and Scotland devolved contexts; as well as (2) Oxfam&apos;s international influencing goals to maximise impact. This work currently focuses primarily (99%) on the Valuing Women&apos;s Work Global Strategy.   The project will broadly aim to influence policies, practices, narratives and values among key decision -makers in private and public sectors, and the general public; and to work closely with partners to support/join their influencing/programmatic activities and achieve shared goals. The project will entail engagement with key stakeholders including people with lived experience, Third Sector organisations and coalitions/civil society movements, as well as potentially strategic alliances with private sector, policy stakeholders and decision -makers at national and local level across the UK (including devolved nations, through coordination with Oxfam Scotland and Wales, and devolved local authorities in England).   This project will host restricted (lightly or fully) funded activities (not unrestricted, which are currently (FY23) hosted in IMPA10.   The project entails and range of activities, many in partnership, including for FY23:  **Oxfam -led:   - Care &amp; poverty evidence review (PPL)  - Narratives research on reframing care work (PPL)  - Contribution to National Outcome on Care campaign in Scotland (PPL)  **grants to partners:  - Grant to We Care Campaign (first and second) (Unwrapped)  - Grant to WiSE for research bid on redistribution of care in HHs (PPL)  - Grant to WEN Wales on caring coalition (Wales to lead/PPL)  - Grant to SWBG on  (Scotland to lead/PPL)  - Carers Week 2022 (Unwrapped)  - contr</narrative>
  </description>
